### Test Synapse Backend API
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension or curl

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. Get all changes (should be empty initially)
GET {{baseUrl}}/changes

### 2. Get blueprints from catalog
GET {{baseUrl}}/blueprints

### 3. Create a new change
POST {{baseUrl}}/changes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "objective": "RESTART_DB_SERVICES",
  "target": "db_servers",
  "domain": "CNTT",
  "constraints": {
    "maintenanceWindow": true
  }
}

### 4. Assess the change (use ID from step 3 response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/changes/CHG-001/assess

### 5. Approve the change
POST {{baseUrl}}/changes/CHG-001/approve

### 6. Resolve execution plan
POST {{baseUrl}}/changes/CHG-001/resolve-plan

### 7. Execute the plan (use planId from step 6 response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/plans/PLAN-001/execute

### 8. Check execution status (use executionId from step 7 response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/executions/EXEC-001/status

### 9. Get execution log
GET {{baseUrl}}/executions/EXEC-001/log

### 10. Get job events (task-level progress)
GET {{baseUrl}}/executions/EXEC-001/events

### 11. Get audit log
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit

### 12. Get audit log for specific change
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit?changeId=CHG-001

### Test Case: Create change WITHOUT maintenance window (should BLOCK)
POST {{baseUrl}}/changes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "objective": "RESTART_DB_SERVICES",
  "target": "db_servers",
  "domain": "CNTT",
  "constraints": {
    "maintenanceWindow": false
  }
}

### Then assess (should get Policy=BLOCK)
POST {{baseUrl}}/changes/CHG-002/assess
